    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test run \u2014 the only test class). \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily registration limit rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100+ owners already have today's `registrationDate`.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `RequireCityCapacity` rule), I added:\n\n- **`RequireDailyRegistrationLimit`** (function step) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; throws `DailyRegistrationLimitException` at \u2265100.\n- **`DailyRegistrationLimitException`** (checked exception).\n- **`DailyRegistrationLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds 429 with a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the other handlers.\n- Escalation YAML `\u2026DailyRegistrationLimitException.yml` mapping the exception to its handler.\n- Wired a `dailyLimit` step into `owners.POST.yml` (between `cityCapacity` and `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`).\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (create 100, expect the 101st to be 429) passes, and the full suite is green.",
